d higher energy density compared to traditional AC systems; Fluence Mosaic, a conventional bidding software; and Fluence Nispera, an asset performance management (APM) software. The company also provides operational and maintenance services; and digital applications. It serves independent power producers, developers, conglomerates, utilities/load-serving entities, and commercial and industrial customers. Fluence Energy, Inc. was founded in 2018 and is headquartered in Arlington, Virginia.","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, improving at 24%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $12K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Fluence Energy, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.0B market cap on $2.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +24% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -28% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 9% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $160M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -90.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 14% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"